1. Dashboard
Overview of Finances:

Show a summarized view of
	income
	expenses
	Savings
	Investments

	for both the rental business and family.
Graphs and Charts: Visualize trends in income and expenses over time, broken down by month, category, or property.


2. Expense and Income Tracking
Add Income/Expense Entries: Form to add and categorize different types of income (rent, salary, etc.) and expenses (maintenance, groceries, etc.).
Categorization: Allow for custom categories such as “Rental Expenses,” “Family Expenses,” “Maintenance,” “Utilities,” etc.
Recurring Entries: Automatically track recurring expenses (like rent payments, utility bills, mortgage) and income (monthly rent, salary).
Search and Filter: Allow users to search transactions by category, date range, or amount.

3. Receipt Management
Upload Receipts: Let users upload receipts for expenses or income. Store images or PDFs of receipts.
Receipt Tagging: Tag receipts with categories like "Rental Property 1" or "Groceries" to easily retrieve them later.
Link Receipts to Transactions: Attach receipts directly to individual income or expense entries.

4. Rental Property Management
Property Profiles: Create profiles for each rental property to track specific income and expenses per property.
Tenant Information: Store tenant details (names, lease dates, contact info, payment history).
Lease Tracking: Keep track of lease start/end dates, rent amounts, and lease renewals.
Rental Invoices: Generate and send invoices to tenants.

5. Family Budgeting
Budgeting Tools: Set monthly budgets for different categories (food, entertainment, education, etc.).
Family Member Profiles: Track income and expenses separately for each family member.
Shared Expenses: Tag expenses as shared (e.g., family vacations, groceries) or individual (e.g., personal purchases).

6. Reports
Monthly/Annual Reports: Generate reports summarizing income, expenses, and profit/loss for both the business and family.
Tax Preparation Reports: Export data to simplify tax filing (breakdowns of expenses, income, and receipts).
Property-Specific Reports: Generate detailed reports for individual rental properties.

7. Notifications and Reminders
Payment Reminders: Automatic reminders for rent collection or upcoming expenses.
Expense Alerts: Get alerts if expenses exceed a set budget.
Lease Renewal Alerts: Notify users when a lease is nearing its end.

8. User Roles and Permissions
Admin/User Roles: Set up different permissions (you as the admin, other family members, or an accountant with limited access).
Multi-User Access: Allow family members to log in and manage their expenses.

9. Mobile-Friendly Interface
Mobile Version: Ensure the app works well on mobile devices for easy expense tracking and receipt uploading on the go.
Offline Functionality: Let users add entries and upload receipts even when offline, syncing when the connection is restored.

10. Data Backup and Security
Cloud Backup: Automatically back up data to the cloud to avoid data loss.
Encryption: Secure sensitive data like financial records and receipts.

11. Integrations
Bank Account Integration: Integrate with bank accounts to automatically import transactions.
Tax Software Export: Export financial data to tax software like QuickBooks or TurboTax.
These features will help you efficiently manage both your rental business and personal finances, making the web application a comprehensive financial management tool.


